      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Again we cannot rely on the shortsightedness from VR Chat, the back end architecture is a joke, the leadership lead with their wallets over safety.  As I reported in Linked In on how companies like VR Chat are more interested in user count over quality of users as a metric of success and attempt to restrict any report of 'Issues' that may say otherwise.\n\nHalf of their issues could have been resolved with simple behavioral analysis in the system logs; but that would require a desire to protect the communities and at least two brain cells.   VR Chat has neither.\n\nLack of care for the community breeds discontent with the users, and some of the users are leaps and bounds more intelligent and skilled enough to produce enough evidence based reporting that can be handed to governmental agencies.   Disney Corp was just found guilty of COPPA violations and sentenced to 10 Million USD for failure to protect children.\n\nI know of someone that has much more evidence of COPPA Violation that could lead to a maximum fine from the FTC of 23 Million USD.  All due cause there is no one that cares enough in the corporation.\n\nPerhaps when the evidence is handed over to the US DOJ that VR Chat may realize that they should have listened to the communities more than they have done in the past.   Assuming the fines do not bankrupt them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
